        <!-- Example traffic callouts -->
        <mxCell id="p2_note_pp" value="&lt;b&gt;ping_pong example&lt;/b&gt; (tiles 0 ↔ 15)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#334155;font-weight:normal&quot;&gt;each turn: WriteUnique to shared line, notify via ChiGem5EventBus; peer wait_on() wakes, reads back. In rnf_l2 the line ping-pongs between leaf caches (SnpUnique); in rni every access crosses to the HN-F.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#1d4ed8;strokeWidth=1.2;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#0f172a;dashed=1;arcSize=5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="1740" width="640" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p2_note_mix" value="&lt;b&gt;Mixed-mode caveat&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#334155;font-weight:normal&quot;&gt;Per-tile mode is possible mechanically — CHI_Tile&apos;s constructor takes a mode string — but the shipped generator (CHI_Tile.make_generator) passes one mode to every tile, so &lt;code&gt;--rn-mode&lt;/code&gt; is currently system-wide. The coloring above illustrates the shape of what a mixed generator would produce.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#ea580c;strokeWidth=1.2;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#0f172a;dashed=1;arcSize=5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="720" y="1740" width="640" height="110" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

